# TypeScript, API and security

- Read `.cursor/rules.md` before changing matching files.
- Preserve strict TypeScript, `noUncheckedIndexedAccess` and `exactOptionalPropertyTypes`.
- Do not use `any`, unsafe assertions or untyped external data.
- Validate every request, environment and persistence boundary with Zod.
- Return explicit DTOs; never leak database rows, SQL, stack traces or secret values.
- Keep secrets in server-only modules and mark sensitive modules with `import "server-only"`.
- Never expose database, S3, session or password material through `NEXT_PUBLIC_*`.
- Require authenticated server sessions and same-origin checks for admin mutations.
- Normalize errors into stable public responses and log only non-sensitive context.
